# Shared OAuth2 client credentials — every upstream service client
# (customer entity, engineering entity, updates, SCIM) authenticates as this
# same app; only each service's base URL and scopes differ.
OAUTH2_CLIENT_ID=
OAUTH2_CLIENT_SECRET=
OAUTH2_TOKEN_URL=

# Customer entity service
CUSTOMER_ENTITY_BASE_URL=
CUSTOMER_ENTITY_SCOPES=

# Request timeouts (Go durations, e.g. 45s, 2m). Optional; all must be > 0. Keeping
# ENTITY_SERVICE_TIMEOUT shorter than REST_WRITE_TIMEOUT is advisable so a clean
# error can be returned, but is not enforced. Defaults are raised from the old 30s server / 25s client so large inline-attachment
# uploads are not cut off.
# REST_READ_TIMEOUT=60s
# REST_WRITE_TIMEOUT=60s
# ENTITY_SERVICE_TIMEOUT=60s

# Engineering entity service (a separate internal service, not this repo's
# entity-service). Optional. When ENGINEERING_ENTITY_BASE_URL is set, "Open Git
# issue" (POST /cases/{id}/github-issues) files the issue through it instead of
# the entity service; unset keeps the entity-service path. Also backs
# GET /health/dependencies (unset reports that dependency as "not_configured").
# Must be an https URL (a path is allowed; startup fails otherwise). Uses the
# shared OAUTH2_* credentials above.
ENGINEERING_ENTITY_BASE_URL=
ENGINEERING_ENTITY_SCOPES=

# Updates service
UPDATES_BASE_URL=
UPDATES_SCOPES=

# SCIM operations service
SCIM_BASE_URL=
SCIM_SCOPES=

# SupportPortalLite (/spl/*) — a full port of digiops-cs's
# apps/support-portal-lite Ballerina backend (being retired), serving the
# Sales/Solutions-Architecture audience alongside this backend's existing
# CS Portal audience. Off by default: leave SPL_ENABLED unset (or any value
# other than a recognized true) and none of the SPL_* variables below are
# read, no /spl/* route is registered, and every existing endpoint is
# completely unaffected. Set SPL_ENABLED=true and every variable below
# becomes required (except SERVICENOW_ESCALATION_TEMPLATE_ID and
# TEAM_SCHEDULE_URL, which default to empty) — see cmd/server/main.go's
# loadSPLConfig for the exact rules.
# SPL_ENABLED=true

# Sales-side entity GraphQL service, ported from modules/entity. Authenticates
# with the shared OAUTH2_CLIENT_ID/SECRET/TOKEN_URL app above, the same one
# every other upstream in this file uses — confirmed this is the same
# client-credentials app SPL's own Config.toml already pointed
# entityAppConfig at. Only the base URL needs a value. The old CS-side entity
# GraphQL service (CS_ENTITY_BASE_URL) is gone: it turned out to be
# ServiceNow itself behind a second, parallel integration, not an
# independent data source — Scan User's user-lock/project-closure-state
# checks and project-contact operations now go through
# CUSTOMER_ENTITY_BASE_URL above like every other CS Portal handler.
# SALES_ENTITY_BASE_URL=

# SupportPortalLite's own access-control env vars (SPL_ALLOWED_GROUPS,
# SPL_ADD_ESCALATION_GROUPS, SPL_DOWNLOAD_ATTACHMENT_GROUPS,
# SPL_USAGE_METRICS_GROUPS -- formerly comma-separated Asgardeo group lists,
# see internal/splauth) are gone: every /spl/* route now goes through the
# same AccessGuard/AUTH_*_ROLES roles-based mechanism as the rest of this
# backend (PermSPLAccess for the blanket audience gate, PermEscalate/
# PermDownloadAttachment/PermUsageMetricsViewer layered on top for the
# handful of endpoints that need a narrower check) -- see the AUTH_*_ROLES
# section above, particularly AUTH_SALES_SOLUTIONS_ROLES,
# AUTH_ESCALATOR_ROLES, AUTH_ATTACHMENT_DOWNLOADER_ROLES, and
# AUTH_USAGE_METRICS_VIEWER_ROLES. SPL_ADD_WORKNOTE_GROUPS was already gone
# before this: the /spl/* worknote route it gated was removed once work
# notes moved onto the shared POST /cases/{id}/comments route (see main.go's
# SPL route registration comment).

# ServiceNow integration — Table API + a custom scoped-app REST API on the
# same host, Basic Auth, ported from modules/operations. Required when
# SPL_ENABLED is on (except ESCALATION_TEMPLATE_ID and TEAM_SCHEDULE_URL,
# which default to empty) — see loadSPLConfig for the exact variable names.
# No SPL_ prefix: ServiceNow is this feature's own upstream, not a concept
# scoped to the caller, so it's named after the service like every other
# integration in this file.

# Google Drive integration — OAuth2 refresh-token grant, used for the
# folder-browsing endpoints, ported from modules/googledrive. No SPL_
# prefix, matching this file's existing convention of naming a service's
# own credentials after the service, not the caller.
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Customer-health/risk tracking — MySQL, ported from modules/risk (the first
# MySQL consumer in this monorepo). DSN form: see
# github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql's DSN docs, e.g.
# "user:password@tcp(host:3306)/dbname?parseTime=true" — parseTime=true is
# required.
# SPL_RISK_MYSQL_DSN=

# csm-notification-service / csm-integration-service (integrations/*). Both
# optional — used only to back GET /health/dependencies today (see that
# handler's own doc comment). Uses the shared OAUTH2_* credentials above.
# Unset leaves that dependency reported as "not_configured".
CSM_NOTIFICATION_SERVICE_BASE_URL=
CSM_NOTIFICATION_SERVICE_SCOPES=
CSM_INTEGRATION_SERVICE_BASE_URL=
CSM_INTEGRATION_SERVICE_SCOPES=

# Dashboard definitions — a directory holding ONE JSON file per dashboard.
# Every *.json in it is a dashboard; the FILENAME IS IGNORED, id/displayName/
# type all come from the file's content. Read once at startup and held in
# memory: there is no per-request disk I/O. A malformed, unreadable or
# duplicate-id file FAILS STARTUP naming the file rather than being skipped —
# a silently dropped dashboard is invisible.
# Points at the committed sample set so a fresh clone starts with
# `cp .env.example .env && go run ./cmd/server` — a missing directory is fatal.
# For a real deployment, copy it and edit your own definitions in:
#   cp -r dashboards.example dashboards   # ./dashboards is gitignored
# then set DASHBOARDS_DIR=./dashboards below.
DASHBOARDS_DIR=./dashboards.example

# Re-read DASHBOARDS_DIR on every request instead of serving the startup
# snapshot, so editing a definition needs no restart. LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY;
# leave unset (or false) everywhere else. A failed re-read keeps serving the
# last known-good definitions and logs the error, so a half-saved file does not
# take the dev server down; the startup load still fails hard either way.
DASHBOARDS_HOT_RELOAD=false

# Optional: a JSON file of presetKey -> literal filter fragment
# ({"field":...,"op":...,"values":...}), shared across every dashboard in
# DASHBOARDS_DIR. A dashboard's own top-level "filterPresets" object (same
# shape) shadows a same-named entry here. Referenced from anywhere a literal
# filter object can appear (a widget's query.filters, an anyOf branch's
# filters, or a PieSlice's own query.filters) via {"preset": "presetKey"} —
# expanded into its literal fragment once, at startup, never visible past
# that. Conventionally named with a leading underscore (e.g. _presets.json)
# so LoadDir does not try to parse it as a dashboard: DASHBOARDS_DIR skips
# any *.json file starting with "_". Unset is legal and means no shared
# presets, same as an unset DASHBOARDS_DIR itself.
# DASHBOARD_PRESETS_FILE=./dashboards.example/_presets.json

# Optional: a JSON file of sectionKey -> {"displayName": "...", "widgets":
# [...]}, the shared, reusable widget sections a dashboard pulls in by name.
# A dashboard references one from its own top-level "includeSections" array:
#   "includeSections": [
#     {"section": "my-work", "idPrefix": "ob_", "position": "start",
#      "extraFilters": [{"preset": "onboarded-projects"}]}
#   ]
# so a section like "My Work" is authored and corrected once instead of being
# copy-pasted into every dashboard and drifting apart. Each include may
# prefix the section's widget ids, override its heading, place it before
# ("start", the default) or after ("end") the dashboard's own widgets, and
# AND extra scoping predicates into every case widget it brings in.
# Expanded into literal widgets at startup, never visible past that. Same
# leading-underscore convention as the presets file, and unset is equally
# legal — it means no shared sections.
# DASHBOARD_SECTIONS_FILE=./dashboards.example/_sections.json

# Team registry — the curated team vocabulary, as
# "teamKey|Display Name|FAMILY|groupId" rows separated by commas. FAMILY and
# groupId are both optional; FAMILY, when given, must be one of CRE-ABT, CRE,
# SRE-ABT or SRE (case insensitive) — anything else fails startup naming the
# row, as does a duplicate team key or display name. Display Name must match
# the team's group name in the backing data source exactly: it is what member
# lookups filter on, so a wrong one resolves zero members silently.
# Resolved ONCE at startup into an in-memory index — POST /teams/search makes
# no upstream call at all. No default: unset means no teams are configured,
# which starts (with a warning) but leaves every team picker and team filter
# empty. The values below are placeholders, not real team names.
CSM_TEAM_REGISTRY="alpha|Alpha Team|CRE-ABT,beta|Beta Team|SRE-ABT,delta|Delta Team|CRE,gamma|Gamma Team"

# Assignable-role allow-list — validates the roleIds user filter and is the
# catalogue POST /roles/search serves, so the picker and the filter cannot
# disagree. Optional; unset uses this exact list.
CSM_USER_ROLES=agent,admin,commenter,customer,customer_admin,partner,partner_admin,internal,external,timecard_approver

# Real role name -> identity-provider role id mapping, a JSON object string.
# Keyed by the role name exactly as it appears in AUTH_<ROLE>_ROLES (not a
# portal-role key like "timecard_approver") -- see directory.ParseRoleIDs's
# own doc comment for why. Lets a handler fetch a role's real membership via
# the SCIM operations service's GET /organizations/internal/roles/{id} (a
# plain get-by-id, not a search by name) -- see GET /users/time-card-approvers
# -- and lets POST /users' own grantRoles field grant a role via SCIM (see
# GET /roles/grantable). Optional overall and per-name: a real name with no
# entry here just means that role has no SCIM-backed feature wired up. The
# value below is a placeholder, not a real role id.
# ASGARDEO_ROLE_IDS={"example-timecard-approver-role":"11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"}

# Which data source the paired entity-service instance is configured with
# (its own DATA_SOURCE) — "servicenow" or "postgres". This backend has no
# other way to know. Optional; defaults to "servicenow". Only matters today
# for validating CSM_ANNOUNCEMENT_EXCLUDED_PROJECT_KEYS below: entity-
# service's Postgres-backed project search does not support excludeProjectKeys,
# so this backend refuses to start if that denylist is set while this is
# "postgres" — every audience search would otherwise fail unconditionally.
CUSTOMER_ENTITY_DATA_SOURCE=servicenow

# Project keys that must never receive an "All customer projects" customer
# announcement — POST /announcements/audience/search injects this list into
# every request unconditionally (the caller cannot opt out), mirroring the
# real ServiceNow flow's own hardcoded Project Key exclusions. Comma-
# separated, whitespace trimmed. Optional; unset excludes nothing extra. The
# values below are placeholders, not real project keys. Requires
# CUSTOMER_ENTITY_DATA_SOURCE=servicenow — see its own comment above.
CSM_ANNOUNCEMENT_EXCLUDED_PROJECT_KEYS=Apexia,Veridian,Veloxis

# Auth — set to false for local testing (skips JWT signature verification)
AUTH_JWKS_ENDPOINT=
AUTH_ISSUER=
AUTH_AUDIENCE=                    # comma-separated; token is accepted if any listed audience is present
AUTH_TOKEN_VALIDATOR_ENABLED=true

# Access control — the token roles that grant each portal role. Each value is a
# comma-separated list of role names; holding any one grants the role. Matching
# is exact and case-sensitive. There is no default: a role whose variable is
# unset or empty is held by nobody, and startup warns naming it. Set these to
# the role names your identity provider puts in the token's "roles" claim.
AUTH_VIEWER_ROLES=
AUTH_ESCALATOR_ROLES=
AUTH_ATTACHMENT_DOWNLOADER_ROLES=
AUTH_SUPPORT_ENGINEER_ROLES=
AUTH_ADMIN_ROLES=
AUTH_USAGE_METRICS_VIEWER_ROLES=
AUTH_TIMECARD_APPROVER_ROLES=
AUTH_DASHBOARD_DESIGNER_ROLES=
# Marker role, not a capability — grants nothing above, gates no route here.
# Reported to the webapp via GET /users/me so it can pick the Sales/
# Solutions-Architecture (SPL) nav over CS Portal's own instead of deciding
# client-side from Asgardeo groups. Unlike the roles above, leaving this
# unset is a normal, supported state (CS Portal alone still works), so
# startup does not warn about it.
AUTH_SALES_SOLUTIONS_ROLES=
# Grants ONLY posting a work_note-type comment on a case (POST
# /cases/{id}/comments) — not a customer-visible reply, and none of
# PermWrite's other actions. CsEngineer/Admin already hold this regardless,
# so leaving it unset just means no additional role can create work notes;
# like AUTH_SALES_SOLUTIONS_ROLES, startup does not warn about it.
AUTH_WORKNOTE_CREATOR_ROLES=
# Who may create and send a customer announcement. Required on top of write
# access, not instead of it: a CS engineer WITHOUT this role can no longer
# create, edit, schedule or publish an announcement (admin always can), and a
# holder who is not a CS engineer or admin still cannot. Set it to the
# Asgardeo role the announcement creators hold before deploying, or only
# admin can create announcements; startup warns while it is unset. Approving
# a request is not gated by it.
AUTH_ANNOUNCEMENT_CREATOR_ROLES=

# SFTPGo-backed attachment storage — off by default. When off (unset/false),
# none of the vars below are read and the /cases/{id}/attachments/upload-token
# and /attachments/{id}/share routes are not even registered; the existing
# streaming attachment endpoints (POST /attachments, GET /attachments/{id}/content,
# DELETE /attachments/{id}) are completely unaffected either way.
# SFTPGO_ATTACHMENT_STORAGE_ENABLED=false
# SFTPGo's REST API base URL. Required when SFTPGO_ATTACHMENT_STORAGE_ENABLED=true.
# SFTPGO_BASE_URL=https://sftpgo.example.com
# Public host for constructing share URLs (/web/client/pubshares/{id}) — set
# this only if SFTPGo's WebClient share pages are fronted separately from its
# REST API. Optional; defaults to SFTPGO_BASE_URL when unset.
# SFTPGO_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# Customer-onboarding status column on a project's Contacts tab — off by
# default. Exactly "true" registers GET /projects/{id}/onboarding-steps (backed
# by the entity service's onboarding ledger via the existing customer entity
# client); unset, empty or any other value leaves the route unregistered and
# changes nothing else. The webapp has a matching window.config key of the
# same name that hides the column and skips the request.
# CSM_MIGRATION_ONBOARDING_STATUS_ENABLED=false

# Server
PORT=8080
